<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>MVC Architecture × Microservices × REST API</title>

  <style>
    *{
      margin:0;
      padding:0;
      box-sizing:border-box;
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    }

    body{
      background:#f4f6f9;
      color:#333;
      line-height:1.6;
    }

    header{
      background:#0f172a;
      color:white;
      text-align:center;
      padding:40px 20px;
    }

    header h1{
      font-size:40px;
      margin-bottom:10px;
    }

    .container{
      width:90%;
      max-width:1100px;
      margin:30px auto;
    }

    .card{
      background:white;
      padding:25px;
      margin-bottom:25px;
      border-radius:12px;
      box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
    }

    .card h2{
      color:#2563eb;
      margin-bottom:15px;
    }

    .code-box{
      background:#111827;
      color:#22c55e;
      padding:15px;
      border-radius:10px;
      overflow-x:auto;
      margin-top:15px;
      font-family: Consolas, monospace;
    }

    ul{
      margin-left:20px;
    }

    .api-table{
      width:100%;
      border-collapse:collapse;
      margin-top:15px;
    }

    .api-table th,
    .api-table td{
      border:1px solid #ccc;
      padding:12px;
      text-align:left;
    }

    .api-table th{
      background:#2563eb;
      color:white;
    }

    footer{
      text-align:center;
      padding:20px;
      background:#0f172a;
      color:white;
      margin-top:40px;
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>

  <header>
    <h1>MVC Architecture × Microservices × REST API</h1>
    <p>Understanding Modern Backend Development</p>
  </header>

  <div class="container">

    <!-- MVC -->
    <div class="card">
      <h2>📦 MVC Architecture</h2>

      <p>
        MVC stands for Model-View-Controller.
        It separates application logic into 3 connected components.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Model</strong> → Handles database and business logic</li>
        <li><strong>View</strong> → User Interface / Frontend</li>
        <li><strong>Controller</strong> → Handles requests and responses</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="code-box">
<pre>
project/
│
├── models/
│   └── UserModel.js
│
├── views/
│   └── userView.html
│
├── controllers/
│   └── UserController.js
│
└── app.js
</pre>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Microservices -->
    <div class="card">
      <h2>⚙️ Microservices Architecture</h2>

      <p>
        Microservices divide an application into small independent services.
        Each service handles a specific business function.
      </p>

      <h3>Example Services:</h3>

      <ul>
        <li>User Service</li>
        <li>Payment Service</li>
        <li>Order Service</li>
        <li>Notification Service</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="code-box">
<pre>
[ Client ]
     |
     v
[ API Gateway ]
     |
--------------------------------
|        |         |           |
v        v         v           v

User   Order    Payment   Notification
Service Service  Service      Service
</pre>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- REST API -->
    <div class="card">
      <h2>🌐 REST API</h2>

      <p>
        REST API allows systems to communicate over HTTP using standard methods.
      </p>

      <table class="api-table">
        <tr>
          <th>Method</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
          <th>Example</th>
        </tr>

        <tr>
          <td>GET</td>
          <td>Retrieve Data</td>
          <td>/users</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
          <td>POST</td>
          <td>Create Data</td>
          <td>/users</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
          <td>PUT</td>
          <td>Update Data</td>
          <td>/users/1</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
          <td>DELETE</td>
          <td>Delete Data</td>
          <td>/users/1</td>
        </tr>
      </table>

      <div class="code-box">
<pre>
// Example REST API Endpoint

app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
   res.json([
      { id: 1, name: "John" },
      { id: 2, name: "Jane" }
   ]);
});
</pre>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <footer>
    <p>© 2026 Backend Development Learning</p>
  </footer>

</body>
</html>
